# Throughline environment.
#
# LOCAL DEV NEEDS NOTHING HERE. `npm install && npm run dev` runs on an in-process
# PGlite database under .data/ with file uploads on the local disk. Every variable below
# is for deployment, or to switch on an optional integration.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Managed Postgres (the Neon free tier is enough). When present the app uses postgres-js
# instead of PGlite and runs migrations under an advisory lock on boot.
# Missing in production => the app falls back to PGlite on an ephemeral disk and every
# deployment loses its data. Always set it.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host/db?sslmode=require

# Secret for signing/hashing sessions, magic-link tokens and share links.
# Generate: openssl rand -base64 32
# APP_SECRET=

# Public base URL used to build magic-link and invite URLs in emails (no trailing slash).
# Missing => emailed links point at the wrong host.
# APP_URL=https://throughline.nicholasnyaung.com

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FILE ATTACHMENTS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Vercel Blob read/write token. REQUIRED ON VERCEL — its filesystem is read-only and
# per-invocation ephemeral, so local-disk uploads would fail or silently vanish.
# Also run: npm install @vercel/blob
# Missing => uploads/downloads use the local filesystem under .data/uploads (correct for
# local dev, broken on serverless).
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — AI. Set at most one; the app auto-detects which.
# Missing both => AI features run a deterministic offline "mock" provider, so board
# generation / summaries / delegation help / chat still respond, just without a real model.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=            # default: gemini-2.5-flash
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=
# NVIDIA_MODEL=            # default: meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — EMAIL
# Missing RESEND_API_KEY => email is a safe no-op: invites and notifications are not
# delivered, and in development the magic link is printed to the server console instead.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# RESEND_API_KEY=
# EMAIL_FROM="Throughline <onboarding@resend.dev>"

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — SCHEDULED AUTOMATIONS
# Missing => GET /api/cron/run-due always returns 403 and "when overdue" automations
# never fire. Everything else works.
#
# The secret must be sent in a HEADER, never a query string (query strings leak into
# proxy/CDN access logs):
#   curl -H "x-cron-secret: $CRON_SECRET" https://<host>/api/cron/run-due
# Vercel Cron (see vercel.json) sends "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" automatically,
# which this endpoint also accepts.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# CRON_SECRET=

# Slack mirroring and outbound webhooks are configured per-workspace in Settings (owner),
# not via env.
